message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper below."
title: "Unlearnable, or Unmeasured? On the Reliability of Difficulty Labels in RLVR"
abstract: >-
  We revisit the unlearnability phenomenon in reinforcement learning with verifiable rewards and
  find that the affected prompts improve at roughly one third of the learnable rate, while the
  difficulty-defined set used to study them is much less reproducible than expected.
